#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sow — emit the argument worlds production inhabits, as test-generator input.

A function is the set of specializations its *production* callers exercise.
Tests are a subtract filter, not a peer: sow does not report test/prod tilts.
It prints the fixture records a generator can turn into tests — production
worlds (and collection members) the existing tests do not already inhabit.

Exit codes:
  0  ok (or --check with no due fixtures)
  1  --check found one or more due fixtures
  2  usage / tool error
"""
